  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Rain comes to an end this morning... \nDry conditions through at least mid-week, with increasing rain\nchances late week.\n\nAn upper shortwave is in the process of passing across the\nregion this morning. As a result, slow-moving downpours with\noccasional lightning are ongoing across Virginia. Rain should \ntaper off by sunrise and skies will gradually clear throughout \nthe day. Warm and humid conditions continue through this evening\nahead of an approaching cold front.\n\nStrong high pressure will build east by Monday, reducing dew\npoints and bringing slightly cooler temperatures to the area.\nThe frontal passage may bring a few showers to the western\nmountains, but elsewhere, any additional rainfall chances remain\nlow. Dry high pressure will persist through at least Wednesday,\nwith increasing chances for scattered showers and storms again\nby Thursday as high pressure breaks down and moisture begins to\nreturn back into the region.",
